---
import SaidDocsLayout from "../../../layouts/SaidDocsLayout.astro";
import SaidShot from "../../../components/SaidShot.astro";
import SaidPlaceholder from "../../../components/SaidPlaceholder.astro";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  name: "Connect your AI agent to your Said desk",
  description:
    "Connect an MCP agent to Said and let it file its own work under its own name.",
  step: [
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Add Said as an MCP server" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Ask for something real" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Work the same card together" },
  ],
};
---

<SaidDocsLayout
  title="Let your agent in — Said guides"
  description="Connect an MCP agent to your Said desk and watch it file its own work under its own name."
  section="guides"
  kicker="Guide 03"
  heading="Let your agent in"
  dek="One line of setup, a named teammate."
  slug="agents-at-the-desk"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    Said speaks MCP — the protocol AI agents use to work with tools. Connected,
    an agent can read your boards, search your notes, file cards, move them, and
    leave notes in card threads. Signed, every time, with its own name.
  </p>

  <h2 id="connect">1 · Connect</h2>
  <pre><code>said mcp</code></pre>
  <p>
    Register that command as a stdio server in your agent's MCP settings —
    whichever assistant you run, it is one line in its config. The agent now
    carries the desk's tools: listing boards, searching, adding and moving
    cards, leaving notes, reading the exact lines a card references.
  </p>

  <h2 id="real-work">2 · Ask for something real</h2>
  <p>
    Tell your agent to sweep your notes for loose ends and file each one as a
    card with a reference to the lines it came from. Then open the board — the
    new cards are there, each naming the agent that made it.
  </p>
  <SaidShot
    src="/said/shots/casefile.png"
    alt="A case file where agent:builder reports its fix in the thread, signed by name"
  />

  <h2 id="together">3 · Work the same card together</h2>
  <p>
    Nobody owns a card. You can be editing while an agent leaves a note; its
    words land in the thread under its name, next to yours. The history keeps
    everyone honest — every move records who, when, and from where. From your
    phone, the remote client shows the same desk the agents are working.
  </p>
  <div style="max-width: 320px;">
    <SaidPlaceholder
      label="Capture coming — the remote client view"
      ratio="9 / 16"
    />
  </div>

  <h2 id="limits">What it can't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It can't edit your markdown — your files aren't its to touch.</li>
    <li>It can't act unasked — an agent works when you set it working.</li>
    <li>It can't hide — there is no anonymous move in this house.</li>
  </ul>
</SaidDocsLayout>
